# Committed git-rerere cache (HLDD-004 §2, §4 step D, §8 step 4).
#
# When a maintainer resolves a rebase conflict locally during the conflict
# runbook (docs/runbooks/conflict-resolution.md), they export the recorded
# resolution from .git/rr-cache into THIS directory and commit it, so the cloud
# pipeline (tools/pipeline/lib/rebase.sh) replays the same resolution on the
# ephemeral runner next time and the rebase stays clean.
#
# Each recorded resolution is a subdirectory named by rerere's conflict hash,
# containing `preimage` and `postimage` files. This .gitkeep just ensures the
# directory exists in a fresh clone (rerere has nothing to replay until the
# first conflict is resolved and committed).
